<title>USA: Federal Express Corp Q2 Nov 30 net rises.</title>
<headline>Federal Express Corp Q2 Nov 30 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>MEMPHIS, Tenn. 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second Quarter Fiscal 1997</p>
<p>(In millions, except earnings per share and operating data)</p>
<p>			   Three Months Ended    Six Months Ended</p>
<p>				November 30	     November 30</p>
<p> FINANCIAL RESULTS	1996	1995	 1996	 1995</p>
<p> Revenues	  $   2,852.4$   2,547.0$   5,544.7$   5,000.4</p>
<p> Operating Expenses  2,667.5     2376.1    5,229.9    4,680.3</p>
<p> Operating Income	184.9	170.9	314.8	320.1</p>
<p> Pretax Income	   180.4	155.0	288.1	284.8</p>
<p> Net Income		103.7	 89.9	165.7	165.2</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share     0.90	 0.78	 1.44	 1.45</p>
<p>Common and Common</p>
<p> Equivalent Shares  115,132    114,520    115,033    113,948</p>
<p>NOTE: The 97 Q2 results include a net gain of $0.11 per share for $12 million in sales of aircraft noise-reduction kits and a $13.5 million benefit from the settlement of a personal property tax matter, the company said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
